## ⚠️ 5. Pitfalls in External Starters & Plugins

1. **Stack Lock-in**: Many popular community starters (e.g. `AIBiz-Automatyzacje/claude-code-starter`) are tightly bound to a specific frontend stack (React 19 + Supabase + Vite). General-purpose engineering workspaces must remain polyglot.
2. **Language Friction & Token Waste**: Templates with non-English filenames or prompts pollute the prompt cache and burn unnecessary context tokens.
3. **Subagent Proliferation**: Running 7+ heavy reviewer subagents on every minor prompt saturates Claude Code's context window. Subagents must be invoked just-in-time (JIT) for non-trivial milestones.
4. **Tautological Mocks**: Mocking out all dependencies in tests gives false confidence. Final verification requires real runtime execution against actual CLI tools or endpoints.

